@.str.139 = private unnamed_addr constant [951 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Download a file to the Nix store:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix store prefetch-file https://releases.nixos.org/nix/nix-2.3.10/nix-2.3.10.tar.xz\0A  Downloaded 'https://releases.nixos.org/nix/nix-2.3.10/nix-2.3.10.tar.xz' to\0A  '/nix/store/vbdbi42hgnc4h7pyqzp6h2yf77kw93aw-source' (hash\0A  'sha256-qKheVd5D0BervxMDbt+1hnTKE2aRWC8XCAwc0SeHt6s=').\0A  ```\0A\0A* Download a file and get the SHA-512 hash:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix store prefetch-file --json --hash-type sha512 \\\0A      https://releases.nixos.org/nix/nix-2.3.10/nix-2.3.10.tar.xz \\\0A    | jq -r .hash\0A  sha512-6XJxfym0TNH9knxeH4ZOvns6wElFy3uahunl2hJgovACCMEMXSy42s69zWVyGJALXTI+86tpDJGlIcAySEKBbA==\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0AThis command downloads the file *url* to the Nix store. It prints out\0Athe resulting store path and the cryptographic hash of the contents of\0Athe file.\0A\0AThe name component of the store path defaults to the last component of\0A*url*, but this can be overridden using `--name`.\0A\0A\00", align 1
